# examples/spec/fastpaxos.cml: Fast Paxos as an abstract model,
# extending the shared consensus base.  It inherits Agreement (at most
# one value chosen) unchanged.
#
# Reference: Leslie Lamport, "Fast Paxos", Distributed Computing 19(2),
#   2006 (MSR-TR-2005-112): the coordinator's rule in Figure 2, the
#   Quorum Requirement of section 3.1, and the TLA+ specification in the
#   appendix (Phase1b, Phase2a with IsPickableVal, Phase2b).
#
# In a fast round acceptors vote for values clients send them directly,
# so different acceptors can vote for different values (a collision).
# A later classic round recovers: its coordinator reads the promises of
# a classic quorum Q, and with k the highest round any member voted in
# and VS the values voted in round k, it proposes
#   - any proposed value, if no member voted (k = 0);
#   - the one value in VS, if there is one;
#   - else a value w in VS for which O4(w) holds: some fast quorum R
#     has every member of R and Q voting w in round k;
#   - else any proposed value.
# This is safe under the Quorum Requirement: (a) any two quorums
# intersect, and (b) any classic quorum and any two fast quorums
# intersect.  With quorums defined by size, Qc classic and Qf fast out
# of N acceptors, (b) is Qc + 2*Qf > 2*N, and it makes O4 hold for at
# most one value.
#
# The instance: N = 3, round 1 fast and round 2 classic, values 1 and 2,
# QC = 2 and QF = 3.  That is the paper's section 3.4.1 choice that
# tolerates the most classic failures at N = 3 (F = 1, E = 0); Qc + 2*Qf
# = 8 > 6.  Every phase 1b message reports a vote from round 1 or none,
# so the coordinator's rule depends only on how many members of Q
# reported each value, and phase2a(v, n0, n1, n2) picks the quorum by
# those counts: n0 members reported no vote, n1 a vote for 1 and n2 a
# vote for 2, each at most the number of such promises received, with
# n0 + n1 + n2 >= QC.  O4(w) for a quorum of size s with n_w votes for w
# holds iff (N - s) + n_w >= qf: the largest fast quorum whose members
# in Q all voted w is everyone outside Q plus Q's votes for w.
#
# Messages: vote1[a] is acceptor a's round 1 vote (0 = none), cnt1b[w]
# counts the round 2 promises that reported w (0 = no vote), val2a is
# round 2's proposal, and vrnd[a] == 2 marks a's round 2 vote.  A
# promise closes round 1 for that acceptor: rnd[a] = 2 disables its fast
# vote.  What is abstracted away: two rounds, one coordinator, no 1a
# messages (round 1 needs no phase 1; a round 2 promise needs no
# trigger), no coordinated or uncoordinated recovery from 2b messages
# (the paper shows it equivalent to phase 1b), no loss or duplication,
# and both values always proposed.  In the BUG case two values can
# satisfy O4, and the rule may pick either; the paper's TLA+ uses CHOOSE
# there, which picks one.
#
# -DBUG: shrink_fast_quorum, enabled before any acceptor acts, sets the
# fast quorum size qf to QFBUG = 2, so the whole protocol (learning and
# the coordinator's O4) runs with Qc + 2*Qf = 6, not more than 2*N.  A
# classic and a fast quorum still intersect; two fast quorums and a
# classic quorum need not.  A value fast-chosen by two acceptors can
# then be overridden by recovery.
#
#   cmc --spec examples/spec/fastpaxos.cml
#   cmc --spec examples/spec/fastpaxos.cml --define BUG   (Qc + 2*Qf <= 2*N)

module fastpaxos
extends consensus

const N = 3                     # acceptors 0 .. N-1
const QC = 2                    # classic quorum size
const QF = 3                    # fast quorum size: QC + 2*QF > 2*N
const QFBUG = 2                 # the BUG's fast quorum: QC + 2*QFBUG = 2*N

# the fast quorum size in force (QF unless the BUG shrinks it at start)
var qf : QFBUG .. QF

# acceptor state: the highest round promised or voted in, and the round
# and value of its last vote (0 = none)
var rnd : [0 .. N-1 -> 0 .. 2]
var vrnd : [0 .. N-1 -> 0 .. 2]
var vval : [0 .. N-1 -> 0 .. V]

# messages: round 1 votes, round 2 promises by reported value, round 2's
# proposal
var vote1 : [0 .. N-1 -> 0 .. V]
var cnt1b : [0 .. V -> 0 .. N]
var val2a : 0 .. V

init qf == QF
init rnd == [a in 0 .. N-1 -> 0]
init vrnd == [a in 0 .. N-1 -> 0]
init vval == [a in 0 .. N-1 -> 0]
init vote1 == [a in 0 .. N-1 -> 0]
init cnt1b == [w in 0 .. V -> 0]
init val2a == 0

# round 1 (fast): acceptor a votes for a client's value v.
action fastvote(a in 0 .. N-1, v in 1 .. V):
  when rnd[a] == 0
  rnd' = [rnd except [a] = 1]
  vrnd' = [vrnd except [a] = 1]
  vval' = [vval except [a] = v]
  vote1' = [vote1 except [a] = v]

# v is chosen in round 1 once a fast quorum voted for it.
action learn_fast(v in 1 .. V):
  when (count a in 0 .. N-1 : vote1[a] == v) >= qf
  chosen' = [chosen except [v] = 1]

# round 2 phase 1b: acceptor a promises round 2, which closes round 1
# for it, and reports its last vote.
action phase1b(a in 0 .. N-1):
  when rnd[a] < 2
  rnd' = [rnd except [a] = 2]
  cnt1b' = [cnt1b except [vval[a]] = cnt1b[vval[a]] + 1]

# round 2 phase 2a: the coordinator's rule (Figure 2) over a classic
# quorum of promises with n0, n1 and n2 members reporting no vote, a
# vote for 1 and a vote for 2.
action phase2a(v in 1 .. V, n0 in 0 .. N, n1 in 0 .. N, n2 in 0 .. N):
  when val2a == 0 and n0 <= cnt1b[0] and n1 <= cnt1b[1] and n2 <= cnt1b[2] and n0 + n1 + n2 >= QC and (n1 + n2 == 0 or (n2 == 0 and v == 1) or (n1 == 0 and v == 2) or (n1 > 0 and n2 > 0 and ((v == 1 and N - (n0 + n1 + n2) + n1 >= qf) or (v == 2 and N - (n0 + n1 + n2) + n2 >= qf) or (N - (n0 + n1 + n2) + n1 < qf and N - (n0 + n1 + n2) + n2 < qf))))
  val2a' = v

# round 2 phase 2b: acceptor a votes for round 2's proposal.
action phase2b(a in 0 .. N-1):
  when val2a != 0 and vrnd[a] < 2
  rnd' = [rnd except [a] = 2]
  vrnd' = [vrnd except [a] = 2]
  vval' = [vval except [a] = val2a]

# v is chosen in round 2 once a classic quorum voted for it.
action learn_classic(v in 1 .. V):
  when val2a == v and (count a in 0 .. N-1 : vrnd[a] == 2) >= QC
  chosen' = [chosen except [v] = 1]

# the planted bug: before anything happens, run with fast quorums of
# QFBUG acceptors.
action shrink_fast_quorum [BUG]:
  when qf == QF and (all a in 0 .. N-1 : rnd[a] == 0)
  qf' = QFBUG
